@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# Recompute checkpoint state containing non-finite floats
+
+Durable checkpoints persist built values as JSON. NaN and positive or negative
+infinity can become `null` during a model's JSON dump or the checkpoint writer.
+Previously, these values were tagged as restorable, leaving their producer built
+on resume even though a downstream component received `None`.
+
+The checkpoint encoder now treats non-finite floats as opaque state. It also
+checks raw Pydantic model fields before a model serializer can replace those
+numbers, and rejects non-finite numbers introduced by a JSON serializer. Nested
+containers use the existing opaque-drop marker. The graph's existing resume
+logic recomputes a dropped producer when an unbuilt downstream vertex needs it.
+Finite values and genuine `None` retain their existing wire format.
+
+This does not change general API output serialization, introduce a new wire
+format, or recover original numeric values from older checkpoints that already
+contain `null`. Recomputing a producer can repeat its side effects, as with other
+opaque checkpoint state; this change does not provide exactly-once execution.
+
+Regression coverage includes scalar and nested values, LFX Data, and connected
+producer/consumer graphs persisted through SQLite and reopened before resume.
